    "decision": "Count [K]s as sure tricks when bidding. It changes the shop value of [K]s against [A]s and conflicts with [K] payoffs.",
    "opponent": "Once revealed, opponents see more [A]s than the deck should allow, and the [K] and [Q] holdings they relied on lose to them.",
    "rationale": "A lower-power sibling of the [2]s version: it makes near-winners certain rather than adding winners, so the pair measures whether certainty or trick count is what makes rank enablers work. It has the same destination but a different source filter, so it is not a signature duplicate.",
